  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: 7 days of fever with sweats\n- Symptoms: Fevers with alternating hot/cold episodes (rigors/chills), night sweats, diffuse myalgias, nausea, poor appetite, reduced fluid intake, fatigue. OTC paracetamol/ibuprofen provide only partial, temporary relief. No cough, sore throat, ear pain, diarrhea, neck stiffness, new/worsening headache, rash, joint swelling, dysuria, urinary frequency, or flank pain.\n- Onset/duration: Began ~7 days ago; patient returned from Vietnam ~4 weeks ago.\n- Past medical history: Chronic back pain (posture-related, in physiotherapy). History of headaches/migraines related to screen use/weather; no other major illnesses reported.\n- Medications: Paroxetine (Seroxat). OTC ibuprofen and paracetamol as per recommended doses during this illness. Took daily malaria prophylaxis while in Vietnam (exact drug unknown).\n- Allergies: Seasonal/pollen (hay fever). No medication allergies reported.\n- Family history: Father died of myocardial infarction at age 68.\n- Social history: Nurse; up to date on vaccinations including Hep B. Non-smoker. Moderate alcohol. Regular moderate exercise. Recent travel: multi-week trip across Vietnam including rural countryside/trekking/cycling in farmland and some cities.\n- Vital signs/exam findings: Not provided (teleconsultation; in-person exam planned).\n- Labs/imaging: None done yet. Planned tests: thick and thin blood films for malaria; inflammatory markers and general blood tests.",
